cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this proof artifact, please cite this archived release."
title: "Squarefree abundant integers at the critical roughness constant"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "mxym"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-28
repository-code: "https://github.com/mxym/math"
url: "https://github.com/mxym/math/tree/release/abundant-roughness-critical-endpoint-v1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  An unconditional proof that, for every fixed A>0, infinitely many odd
  squarefree abundant consecutive-prime products beginning at p have logarithm
  at most p^2-Ap^(3/2). The artifact contains the proof, bounded prior-art
  comparison, an independent-audit record, and a finite identity checker.
keywords:
  - abundant numbers
  - rough numbers
  - Mertens product
  - prime number theorem
  - analytic number theory
